; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
;
; TokenDump — our half of the SCANNER yardstick's dump, moved out of the program.
;
; ★★★ THE FILE'S NAME REACHES THE SCANNER, THROUGH EXACTLY ONE BIT, and the caller
; owes it. The parser derives the language variant from the script kind
; (`getLanguageVariant`) and hands it over in initializeState; there is no parser
; here, so the driver asks the same question — and the answer that matters is the
; unobvious one: **ScriptKindJSON selects the JSX variant**, under which `</` is ONE
; token. Scan a `.json` unit as a `.ts` one and the two yardsticks disagree about
; the same file for a reason neither dump shows.
;
; ★★ THE UNPORTED REPORT BREAKS THE LOOP AND IS PRINTED IN PLACE, which is not the
; same as returning it: a scanner that met something it cannot scan has produced
; every token before that point correctly, and those lines are a comparison worth
; making. The runner reads the first field only.
;
; ★ Moved here in slice 58 for AstDump's reason — one body, two drivers.

use scaly.memory.Page
use scaly.containers.String
use scaly.containers.StringBuilder
use scaly.os.Console
use tscaly.scanner.Scanner

define TokenDump
{
    procedure write(host: ref[Page], mutable text: String, jsx: bool) io linked




























}
